<Layout>
<section class="hero wrap"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="rule"></span> AN OPEN WORKFLOW FOR THOUGHTFUL DEVELOPMENT <span class="index">001 / 考え</span></div><div class="hero-grid"><div><p class="japanese">考えることを、大切に。</p><h1>Think with AI.<br /><em>Not through AI.</em></h1></div><div class="hero-aside"><p>AI can help you build faster. Kangae helps you keep the part that makes you better: the thinking.</p><a class="text-link" href="/product/">Explore the approach <span>↗</span></a></div></div><div class="hero-rule"><span>UNDERSTAND</span><span>ATTEMPT</span><span>REFLECT</span></div></section>
<section class="statement"><div class="wrap statement-grid"><div class="section-tag">01 / THE IDEA</div><div><h2>Keep your hands<br />on the thinking.</h2><p>Good tools remove friction. But not every kind of friction should disappear. Kangae is a portable set of instructions and workflows that encourages active reasoning, experimentation, and judgment while you work with an AI assistant.</p><p>It doesn't ban generated code. It helps you choose when to learn, when to investigate, and when to delegate.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap section-pad"><div class="section-top"><span class="section-tag">02 / A DIFFERENT KIND OF ASSISTANCE</span><span class="tiny">THREE WAYS TO STAY ENGAGED</span></div><div class="principles"><article><span class="number">01</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Make decisions, test hypotheses, and own the code you ship.</p></article><article><span class="number">02</span><h3>Study</h3><p>Practice recall, prediction, and understanding before revealing answers.</p></article><article><span class="number">03</span><h3>Review</h3><p>Challenge assumptions and use AI feedback as evidence, not authority.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="wrap feature-panel"><div><span class="section-tag">03 / THE PRACTICE</span><h2>Help that meets<br />you where you are.</h2><p>Ask for a hint. Try it yourself. Get unstuck. Or delegate deliberately. Kangae adapts to the task without turning every interaction into a lesson.</p><a class="button-dark" href="/product/">See how it works <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="conversation" aria-label="Example Kangae conversation"><div class="conversation-head"><span>FIELD NOTES / 01</span><span>GUIDED UNDERSTANDING</span></div><div class="message"><span>YOU</span><p>Can you help me understand why this component rerenders?</p></div><div class="message assistant-message"><span>KANGAE-ALIGNED ASSISTANCE</span><p>Let's trace what changes first. Which prop or state value do you think triggers the render?</p></div><div class="conversation-foot">THE GOAL ISN'T TO WITHHOLD THE ANSWER. IT'S TO HELP YOU OWN IT.</div></div></section>
<section class="wrap closing"><span class="section-tag">04 / BEGIN</span><h2>Bring your curiosity.<br /><em>Keep your agency.</em></h2><p>One portable folder. No account, service, or required platform.</p><a class="button-dark" href="/docs/first-session/">Start your first session ↗</a><p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/kalebberry/Kangae#how-to-use-kangae">Browse the source on GitHub ↗</a></p></section>
</Layout>